  concept: "Authored objective: Capacitor Charged.\nAuthored requirement: Verify
    the capacitor has charged to at least 95% of the 5 V supply. voltage \u2265 4.75
    V. voltage \u2264 5.1 V. Connection pair C_STORE_Input and C_STORE_Output.\nGeneral
    teaching principle: Capacitor voltage and current vary with circuit state; transient
    observations need a stated time and reference.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game
    evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A storage tank illustrates temporary storage, but electrical capacitance
    has precise circuit equations.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A transient reading is not automatically a settled reading.
